{"timestamp": "2025-07-23T23:02:25.991296", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  total_reward = 0.0\n\n  # Get the integer index for the item to be crafted\n  # The `item` input is a string (e.g., \"PLANK\").\n  target_item_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n\n  # Retrieve the crafting recipe details for the target item.\n  recipe_details = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(target_item_idx)\n\n  if recipe_details is None:\n      # If no recipe is found for the item, it cannot be crafted by this function's logic.\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Identify the specific workshop required for crafting this item.\n  # Recipes typically contain an \"_at\" key specifying the workshop name (e.g., \"workshop1\").\n  workshop_name = recipe_details.get(\"_at\")\n  \n  # If no workshop is specified in the recipe, it's assumed to be not craftable via this\n  # mechanism, or is a primitive that cannot be \"crafted\" in the traditional sense here.\n  # For the given Craft environment, most crafting tasks require a workshop.\n  if workshop_name is None:\n      return total_reward\n\n  workshop_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n\n  # Locate the workshop's coordinates on the current grid.\n  workshop_coords = None\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  # WIDTH and HEIGHT are global constants from the Craft environment definition.\n  for x_coord in range(WIDTH):\n      for y_coord in range(HEIGHT):\n          if grid[x_coord, y_coord, workshop_idx] == 1:\n              workshop_coords = (x_coord, y_coord)\n              break\n      if workshop_coords:\n          break\n\n  if workshop_coords is None:\n      # If the required workshop is not present in the current environment scenario.\n      return total_reward\n\n  ws_x, ws_y = workshop_coords\n\n  # Define potential approach configurations: (target_x, target_y, required_facing_direction)\n  # The agent needs to be on an adjacent square AND facing the workshop.\n  # DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT are global constants from the Craft environment definition.\n  approach_configs = [\n      (ws_x, ws_y - 1, UP),    # Stand below the station, face UP\n      (ws_x - 1, ws_y, RIGHT), # Stand to the left of the station, face RIGHT\n      (ws_x, ws_y + 1, DOWN),  # Stand above the station, face DOWN\n      (ws_x + 1, ws_y, LEFT)   # Stand to the right of the station, face LEFT\n  ]\n\n  station_reached_and_oriented = False\n\n  # Try each approach configuration until one is successful or all fail.\n  for target_px, target_py, target_d in approach_configs:\n      # First, try to move the agent to the `(target_px, target_py)` position.\n      # A simple greedy approach for movement.\n      path_stuck_count = 0 # To detect if agent gets stuck due to obstacles\n      max_stuck_attempts = 5 # If agent can't move for this many steps, assume path is blocked\n\n      while env._current_state.pos != (target_px, target_py) and env.steps < env.max_steps:\n          current_x, current_y = env._current_state.pos\n          action_to_take = -1\n\n          # Greedy movement: prioritize reducing the largest distance component\n          if abs(target_px - current_x) > abs(target_py - current_y):\n              if target_px > current_x:\n                  action_to_take = RIGHT\n              elif target_px < current_x:\n                  action_to_take = LEFT\n          else: # abs(target_py - current_y) >= abs(target_px - current_x)\n              if target_py > current_y:\n                  action_to_take = UP\n              elif target_py < current_y:\n                  action_to_take = DOWN\n\n          # This check handles cases where action_to_take might not be determined (e.g., already on target for one axis)\n          if action_to_take == -1:\n              break # Agent is already at or very close, exit movement loop\n\n          prev_pos = env._current_state.pos\n          reward_step, done_step, _ = env.step(action_to_take)\n          total_reward += reward_step\n\n          if done_step:\n              return total_reward # Environment terminated (e.g., max_steps reached)\n\n          if env._current_state.pos == prev_pos:\n              # Agent did not move, likely due to an obstacle. Increment stuck counter.\n              path_stuck_count += 1\n              if path_stuck_count >= max_stuck_attempts:\n                  break # This path is effectively blocked, try next approach config.\n          else:\n              path_stuck_count = 0 # Reset if agent moved successfully\n\n      # If the agent failed to reach the target position for this config, try the next one\n      if env._current_state.pos != (target_px, target_py):\n          continue # Go to the next `approach_config`\n\n      # Second, orient the agent to face the crafting station (`target_d`).\n      spins_count = 0\n      # A \"move\" action in a direction where the target tile is blocked will still\n      # change the agent's direction. Max 4 spins ensure all cardinal directions are tried.\n      while env._current_state.dir != target_d and spins_count < 4 and env.steps < env.max_steps:\n          reward_spin, done_spin, _ = env.step(target_d) # Try to move in target_d, if blocked, just rotate\n          total_reward += reward_spin\n          spins_count += 1\n          if done_spin:\n              return total_reward # Environment terminated\n\n      # If successfully reached the position AND oriented correctly\n      if env._current_state.dir == target_d:\n          station_reached_and_oriented = True\n          break # Break from the `for approach_configs` loop as a suitable position is found\n\n  # If no suitable crafting station approach point was found or reachable after trying all configs\n  if not station_reached_and_oriented:\n      return total_reward # Cannot reach or orient to the workshop for crafting.\n\n  # Finally, perform the USE action to attempt crafting.\n  # This action will only succeed if the agent is at the correct location,\n  # facing the correct object, and has all required ingredients in inventory.\n  # The environment's _get_reward function will determine the specific reward.\n  if env.steps >= env.max_steps:\n      return total_reward # Ran out of steps before crafting\n\n  reward_use, done_use, _ = env.step(USE)\n  total_reward += reward_use\n  \n  # If the environment indicates `done` after the USE action, return immediately.\n  if done_use:\n      return total_reward\n\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-23T23:03:23.609193", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  total_reward = 0.0\n\n  # Get the integer index for the item to be crafted\n  # The `item` input is a string (e.g., \"PLANK\").\n  target_item_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n\n  # Retrieve the crafting recipe details for the target item.\n  recipe_details = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(target_item_idx)\n\n  if recipe_details is None:\n      # If no recipe is found for the item, it cannot be crafted by this function's logic.\n      # This could happen if the item is a primitive or doesn't exist in recipes.\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Identify the specific workshop required for crafting this item.\n  # Recipes typically contain an \"_at\" key specifying the workshop name (e.g., \"workshop1\").\n  workshop_name = recipe_details.get(\"_at\")\n  \n  # If no workshop is specified, this item might not be craftable at a station\n  # or might be a primitive. Our 'craft' function assumes station-based crafting.\n  if workshop_name is None:\n      return total_reward\n\n  workshop_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n\n  # Locate the workshop's coordinates on the current grid.\n  workshop_coords = None\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  # WIDTH and HEIGHT are global constants from the Craft environment definition.\n  for x_coord in range(WIDTH):\n      for y_coord in range(HEIGHT):\n          if grid[x_coord, y_coord, workshop_idx] == 1:\n              workshop_coords = (x_coord, y_coord)\n              break\n      if workshop_coords:\n          break\n\n  if workshop_coords is None:\n      # If the required workshop is not present in the current environment scenario.\n      return total_reward\n\n  ws_x, ws_y = workshop_coords\n\n  # Define potential approach configurations: (target_x, target_y, required_facing_direction)\n  # The agent needs to be on an adjacent square AND facing the workshop.\n  # DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT are global constants from the Craft environment definition.\n  approach_configs = [\n      (ws_x, ws_y - 1, UP),    # Stand below the station, face UP\n      (ws_x - 1, ws_y, RIGHT), # Stand to the left of the station, face RIGHT\n      (ws_x, ws_y + 1, DOWN),  # Stand above the station, face DOWN\n      (ws_x + 1, ws_y, LEFT)   # Stand to the right of the station, face LEFT\n  ]\n\n  station_reached_and_oriented = False\n  \n  for target_px, target_py, target_d in approach_configs:\n      # First, try to move the agent to the `(target_px, target_py)` position.\n      # A simple greedy approach for movement.\n      path_stuck_count = 0 \n      max_stuck_attempts = 5 # If agent can't move for this many steps, assume path is blocked\n\n      # Simulate movement towards the target position\n      while env._current_state.pos != (target_px, target_py) and env.steps < env.max_steps:\n          current_x, current_y = env._current_state.pos\n          action_to_take = -1 # Initialize with an invalid action\n\n          # Determine the best cardinal direction to move\n          if abs(target_px - current_x) > abs(target_py - current_y):\n              # Prioritize horizontal movement if x-distance is greater\n              if target_px > current_x:\n                  action_to_take = RIGHT\n              elif target_px < current_x:\n                  action_to_take = LEFT\n          else: \n              # Prioritize vertical movement if y-distance is greater or equal\n              if target_py > current_y:\n                  action_to_take = UP\n              elif target_py < current_y:\n                  action_to_take = DOWN\n          \n          # If both x and y are already at target or no valid move determined\n          if action_to_take == -1: \n              break # Agent is effectively at the target or stuck in a corner\n\n          prev_pos = env._current_state.pos\n          reward_step, done_step, _ = env.step(action_to_take)\n          total_reward += reward_step\n\n          if done_step:\n              return total_reward # Environment terminated (e.g., max_steps reached)\n\n          if env._current_state.pos == prev_pos:\n              # Agent did not move, likely due to an obstacle. Increment stuck counter.\n              path_stuck_count += 1\n              if path_stuck_count >= max_stuck_attempts:\n                  # This path is effectively blocked. Break to try next approach config.\n                  break \n          else:\n              # Agent moved successfully, reset stuck counter\n              path_stuck_count = 0 \n      \n      # Check if the agent successfully reached the target position for this config\n      if env._current_state.pos != (target_px, target_py):\n          # If not reached, this approach config failed. Try the next one.\n          continue \n\n      # Second, orient the agent to face the crafting station (`target_d`).\n      # If the agent is already facing the correct direction, this loop won't run.\n      # Otherwise, it will take steps (which might just be rotations if the target square is blocked).\n      spins_count = 0\n      max_spins = 4 # At most 4 spins to try all cardinal directions\n\n      while env._current_state.dir != target_d and spins_count < max_spins and env.steps < env.max_steps:\n          # Stepping in a direction where the cell is occupied results in a rotation.\n          reward_spin, done_spin, _ = env.step(target_d) \n          total_reward += reward_spin\n          spins_count += 1\n          if done_spin:\n              return total_reward # Environment terminated\n\n      # If successfully reached the position AND oriented correctly\n      if env._current_state.dir == target_d:\n          station_reached_and_oriented = True\n          break # Break from the `for approach_configs` loop as a suitable position is found\n\n  # If no suitable crafting station approach point was found or reachable after trying all configs\n  if not station_reached_and_oriented:\n      return total_reward # Cannot reach or orient to the workshop for crafting.\n\n  # Finally, perform the USE action to attempt crafting.\n  # This action will only succeed if the agent is at the correct location,\n  # facing the correct object, and has all required ingredients in inventory.\n  # The environment's _get_reward function will determine the specific reward.\n  if env.steps >= env.max_steps:\n      return total_reward # Ran out of steps before crafting\n\n  reward_use, done_use, _ = env.step(USE)\n  total_reward += reward_use\n  \n  # If the environment indicates `done` after the USE action, return immediately.\n  if done_use:\n      return total_reward\n\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-23T23:03:24.691392", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  total_reward = 0.0\n\n  # 1. Get the integer index for the item to be crafted\n  # The `item` input is a string (e.g., \"PLANK\").\n  target_item_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n\n  # Retrieve the crafting recipe details for the target item.\n  recipe_details = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(target_item_idx)\n\n  if recipe_details is None:\n      # If no recipe is found for the item, it cannot be crafted by this function's logic.\n      # This typically means the item is a primitive or not craftable via recipes.\n      return total_reward\n\n  # 2. Identify the specific workshop required for crafting this item.\n  # Recipes typically contain an \"_at\" key specifying the workshop name (e.g., \"workshop1\").\n  workshop_name = recipe_details.get(\"_at\")\n  \n  # If no workshop is specified in the recipe, it's assumed to be not craftable via this\n  # mechanism (e.g., it might be crafted without a station, or is a primitive resource).\n  # For this Craft environment, most crafting tasks require a workshop.\n  if workshop_name is None:\n      return total_reward\n\n  workshop_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n\n  # 3. Locate the workshop's coordinates on the current grid.\n  workshop_coords = None\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  # Iterate through the grid to find the workshop's position\n  for x_coord in range(WIDTH):\n      for y_coord in range(HEIGHT):\n          # Check if the workshop's one-hot index is set at this grid cell\n          if grid[x_coord, y_coord, workshop_idx] == 1:\n              workshop_coords = (x_coord, y_coord)\n              break\n      if workshop_coords: # Found the workshop, break outer loop\n          break\n\n  if workshop_coords is None:\n      # If the required workshop is not present in the current environment scenario.\n      return total_reward\n\n  ws_x, ws_y = workshop_coords\n\n  # 4. Define potential approach configurations: (target_x, target_y, required_facing_direction)\n  # The agent needs to be on an adjacent square AND facing the workshop.\n  approach_configs = [\n      (ws_x, ws_y - 1, UP),    # Stand below the station, face UP\n      (ws_x - 1, ws_y, RIGHT), # Stand to the left of the station, face RIGHT\n      (ws_x, ws_y + 1, DOWN),  # Stand above the station, face DOWN\n      (ws_x + 1, ws_y, LEFT)   # Stand to the right of the station, face LEFT\n  ]\n\n  station_reached_and_oriented = False\n\n  # Try each approach configuration until one is successful or all fail.\n  for target_px, target_py, target_d in approach_configs:\n      # First, try to move the agent to the `(target_px, target_py)` position.\n      # A simple greedy approach for movement.\n      path_stuck_count = 0 \n      max_stuck_attempts = 5 # If agent can't move for this many steps, assume path is blocked\n\n      # Loop until agent reaches target position or gets stuck or max_steps reached\n      while env._current_state.pos != (target_px, target_py) and env.steps < env.max_steps:\n          current_x, current_y = env._current_state.pos\n          action_to_take = -1\n\n          # Greedy movement: prioritize reducing the largest distance component\n          if abs(target_px - current_x) > abs(target_py - current_y):\n              if target_px > current_x:\n                  action_to_take = RIGHT\n              elif target_px < current_x:\n                  action_to_take = LEFT\n          else: # abs(target_py - current_y) >= abs(target_px - current_x) or they are equal\n              if target_py > current_y:\n                  action_to_take = UP\n              elif target_py < current_y:\n                  action_to_take = DOWN\n              # If agent is already at the target position, action_to_take remains -1,\n              # which will cause the loop to break.\n\n          if action_to_take == -1: # Agent is already at the target position, or an axis is aligned\n              break # Exit movement loop for this configuration\n\n          prev_pos = env._current_state.pos\n          reward_step, done_step, _ = env.step(action_to_take)\n          total_reward += reward_step\n\n          if done_step:\n              return total_reward # Environment terminated (e.g., max_steps reached)\n\n          if env._current_state.pos == prev_pos:\n              # Agent did not move, likely due to an obstacle. Increment stuck counter.\n              path_stuck_count += 1\n              if path_stuck_count >= max_stuck_attempts:\n                  # This path is effectively blocked. Break to try the next approach config.\n                  break \n          else:\n              path_stuck_count = 0 # Reset stuck counter if agent moved successfully\n\n      # If the agent failed to reach the target position for this config, try the next one\n      if env._current_state.pos != (target_px, target_py):\n          continue # Go to the next `approach_config` in the outer loop\n\n      # Second, orient the agent to face the crafting station (`target_d`).\n      # A \"move\" action in a direction where the target tile is blocked will still\n      # change the agent's direction. Max 4 spins ensure all cardinal directions are tried.\n      spins_count = 0\n      while env._current_state.dir != target_d and spins_count < 4 and env.steps < env.max_steps:\n          # Attempt to move in the `target_d` direction. If blocked, agent rotates.\n          reward_spin, done_spin, _ = env.step(target_d)\n          total_reward += reward_spin\n          spins_count += 1\n          if done_spin:\n              return total_reward # Environment terminated\n\n      # If successfully reached the position AND oriented correctly for this configuration\n      if env._current_state.dir == target_d:\n          station_reached_and_oriented = True\n          break # Break from the `for approach_configs` loop as a suitable position is found\n\n  # If no suitable crafting station approach point was found or reachable after trying all configs\n  if not station_reached_and_oriented:\n      return total_reward # Cannot reach or orient to the workshop for crafting.\n\n  # 5. Finally, perform the USE action to attempt crafting.\n  # This action will only succeed if the agent is at the correct location,\n  # facing the correct object, and has all required ingredients in inventory.\n  # The environment's _get_reward function will determine the specific reward.\n  if env.steps >= env.max_steps:\n      return total_reward # Ran out of steps before attempting the final action\n\n  reward_use, done_use, _ = env.step(USE)\n  total_reward += reward_use\n  \n  # If the environment indicates `done` after the USE action, return immediately.\n  if done_use:\n      return total_reward\n\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-23T23:04:34.734539", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  # Constants defined locally to ensure \"no code outside of it\"\n  # These are taken directly from the Craft environment code base.\n  WIDTH = 12\n  HEIGHT = 12\n\n  DOWN = 0\n  UP = 1\n  LEFT = 2\n  RIGHT = 3\n  USE = 4\n\n  total_reward = 0.0\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # 1. Get the item's index from the cookbook and retrieve its recipe.\n  # The 'item' argument is expected to be a string name (e.g., \"plank\", \"axe\").\n  # The cookbook.index[] converts these names to integer indices.\n  item_idx = cookbook.index[item]\n  \n  # If there's no recipe for the requested item (e.g., it's a primitive or unknown),\n  # it cannot be crafted via this process.\n  if item_idx not in cookbook.recipes:\n      return total_reward\n\n  recipe = cookbook.recipes[item_idx]\n\n  # 2. Check if the agent possesses all necessary ingredients for the recipe.\n  current_state = env._current_state # Get the current state of the environment\n  ingredients_ok = True\n  for ingredient_idx, count in recipe.items():\n      # Ingredients are identified by integer indices; special keys like \"_at\" are strings.\n      if isinstance(ingredient_idx, int):\n          if current_state.inventory[ingredient_idx] < count:\n              ingredients_ok = False\n              break\n  \n  # If ingredients are missing, crafting cannot proceed.\n  if not ingredients_ok:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # 3. Identify the specific workshop required for crafting this item.\n  # Recipes typically have an \"_at\" key specifying the required workshop type.\n  if \"_at\" not in recipe:\n      # If no specific workshop is indicated in the recipe, this crafting logic does not apply.\n      return total_reward \n\n  workshop_name = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  workshop_idx = cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n\n  # 4. Locate the workshop's position on the grid.\n  workshop_pos = None\n  # Iterate over the entire grid to find the exact (x, y) coordinates of the workshop.\n  for x_grid in range(WIDTH):\n      for y_grid in range(HEIGHT):\n          if current_state.grid[x_grid, y_grid, workshop_idx] == 1:\n              workshop_pos = (x_grid, y_grid)\n              break # Workshop found, exit inner loop\n      if workshop_pos: # Workshop found, exit outer loop\n          break\n  \n  # If the required workshop is not present in the current grid, crafting is impossible.\n  if not workshop_pos:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # 5. Pathfinding to an empty cell adjacent to the workshop, ensuring the agent faces it correctly.\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # Define possible movement actions and their corresponding (dx, dy) vectors.\n  move_actions_map = {\n      DOWN: (0, -1),\n      UP: (0, 1),\n      LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n  \n  # Determine all valid target cells adjacent to the workshop, and the direction\n  # the agent needs to face from each of those cells to interact with the workshop.\n  target_adj_cells_info = [] # Stores: ((adj_x, adj_y), required_facing_dir)\n  for dx, dy in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]: # Check all four direct neighbors\n      adj_x, adj_y = workshop_pos[0] + dx, workshop_pos[1] + dy\n      \n      # Determine the direction the agent needs to face to interact with the workshop\n      # when standing at (adj_x, adj_y).\n      required_facing_dir = None\n      if dx == -1: # If adjacent cell is to the left of the workshop, agent must face RIGHT.\n          required_facing_dir = RIGHT \n      elif dx == 1: # If adjacent cell is to the right of the workshop, agent must face LEFT.\n          required_facing_dir = LEFT \n      elif dy == -1: # If adjacent cell is below the workshop, agent must face UP.\n          required_facing_dir = UP   \n      elif dy == 1: # If adjacent cell is above the workshop, agent must face DOWN.\n          required_facing_dir = DOWN \n      \n      # Check if the adjacent cell is within grid bounds.\n      is_within_bounds = (0 <= adj_x < WIDTH and 0 <= adj_y < HEIGHT)\n      if is_within_bounds:\n          # Check if the cell is completely empty (no items, including boundaries).\n          is_empty_cell = not current_state.grid[adj_x, adj_y, :].any()\n          \n          if is_empty_cell: # If the cell is empty, it's a valid candidate for movement.\n              target_adj_cells_info.append(((adj_x, adj_y), required_facing_dir))\n\n  # If no valid adjacent and empty cells are found, cannot reach the workshop for crafting.\n  if not target_adj_cells_info:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to an\n  # appropriate crafting spot (adjacent cell with correct orientation).\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position_tuple, list_of_actions_to_reach_here, agent_direction_at_this_position)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [], current_state.dir)])\n  # The visited set stores: ((position_x, position_y), agent_direction_at_that_pos)\n  # This prevents redundant exploration of the same state (position + direction).\n  visited = {(start_pos, current_state.dir)} \n\n  path_to_craft_spot = None # This will store (list_of_actions, final_required_direction_at_craft_spot)\n\n  while queue:\n      (x, y), path, agent_dir = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current (position, direction) matches any of our target crafting spots.\n      for (target_x, target_y), required_dir in target_adj_cells_info:\n          if (x, y) == (target_x, target_y) and agent_dir == required_dir:\n              path_to_craft_spot = (path, required_dir)\n              break # Found a valid path, exit inner loop\n      if path_to_craft_spot:\n          break # Found a valid path, exit outer BFS loop\n\n      # Explore possible next moves (actions) from the current state.\n      for action, (dx, dy) in move_actions_map.items():\n          # Calculate the *intended* next position after taking 'action'.\n          intended_next_x, intended_next_y = x + dx, y + dy\n          \n          # Simulate the outcome of taking 'action':\n          # The agent's direction always changes to the 'action' taken.\n          sim_next_dir = action \n\n          # Determine the actual next position based on game rules (movement blocking).\n          # By default, the agent stays in its current position if the move is blocked.\n          actual_next_pos = (x, y) \n\n          is_intended_pos_valid = (0 <= intended_next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= intended_next_y < HEIGHT)\n          if is_intended_pos_valid:\n              # Movement is blocked if the intended target cell is occupied by any object (including boundaries).\n              is_intended_pos_occupied = current_state.grid[intended_next_x, intended_next_y, :].any()\n              \n              if not is_intended_pos_occupied:\n                  actual_next_pos = (intended_next_x, intended_next_y) # Agent successfully moves.\n          # If `is_intended_pos_valid` is false, it means the move is out of bounds, so the agent stays put.\n\n          # If this simulated new state (actual_next_pos + sim_next_dir) hasn't been visited, add it to the queue.\n          if (actual_next_pos, sim_next_dir) not in visited:\n              visited.add((actual_next_pos, sim_next_dir))\n              queue.append((actual_next_pos, path + [action], sim_next_dir))\n\n  # If no path to a valid crafting spot (with correct orientation) was found,\n  # the crafting cannot be performed. Return the current total_reward (which is 0).\n  if not path_to_craft_spot:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Extract the sequence of actions to take from the found path.\n  path_actions, _ = path_to_craft_spot\n\n  # 6. Execute the determined movement actions in the environment.\n  # Accumulate rewards from each step. The `env.step` function internally updates `env._current_state`.\n  for action in path_actions:\n      reward, _, _ = env.step(action)\n      total_reward += reward\n\n  # At this point, the agent is at the correct position adjacent to the workshop\n  # and is facing the correct direction, as determined by the BFS.\n\n  # 7. Execute the USE action to perform the crafting.\n  reward, _, _ = env.step(USE)\n  total_reward += reward\n\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-23T23:04:35.803330", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  import collections\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Constants defined locally to ensure \"no code outside of it\"\n  WIDTH = 12\n  HEIGHT = 12\n\n  DOWN = 0\n  UP = 1\n  LEFT = 2\n  RIGHT = 3\n  USE = 4\n\n  total_reward = 0.0\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # 1. Get the item's index from the cookbook and retrieve its recipe.\n  # The 'item' argument is expected to be a string name (e.g., \"plank\", \"axe\").\n  # The cookbook.index[] converts these names to integer indices.\n  item_idx = cookbook.index[item]\n  \n  # If there's no recipe for the requested item, it cannot be crafted.\n  if item_idx not in cookbook.recipes:\n      return total_reward\n\n  recipe = cookbook.recipes[item_idx]\n\n  # 2. Check if the agent possesses all necessary ingredients for the recipe.\n  current_state = env._current_state # Get the current state of the environment\n  ingredients_ok = True\n  for ingredient_idx, count in recipe.items():\n      # Ingredients are identified by integer indices; special keys like \"_at\" are strings.\n      if isinstance(ingredient_idx, int):\n          if current_state.inventory[ingredient_idx] < count:\n              ingredients_ok = False\n              break\n  \n  # If ingredients are missing, crafting cannot proceed.\n  if not ingredients_ok:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # 3. Identify the specific workshop required for crafting this item.\n  # Recipes typically have an \"_at\" key specifying the workshop.\n  if \"_at\" not in recipe:\n      # If no workshop is specified, this crafting logic does not apply.\n      return total_reward \n\n  workshop_name = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  workshop_idx = cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n\n  # 4. Locate the workshop's position on the grid.\n  workshop_pos = None\n  for x_grid in range(WIDTH):\n      for y_grid in range(HEIGHT):\n          # Check if the workshop object exists at this (x,y) location\n          # The grid uses one-hot encoding, so `== 1` at the specific index is correct.\n          if current_state.grid[x_grid, y_grid, workshop_idx] == 1:\n              workshop_pos = (x_grid, y_grid)\n              break\n      if workshop_pos: # Workshop found, exit outer loop\n          break\n  \n  # If the required workshop is not present in the current grid, crafting is impossible.\n  if not workshop_pos:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # 5. Pathfinding to an empty cell adjacent to the workshop, ensuring the agent faces it correctly.\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Initial direction of the agent\n  \n  # Define possible movement actions and their corresponding (dx, dy) vectors.\n  move_actions_map = {\n      DOWN: (0, -1),\n      UP: (0, 1),\n      LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n  \n  # Determine all valid target cells adjacent to the workshop, and the direction\n  # the agent needs to face from each of those cells to interact with the workshop.\n  target_adj_cells_info = [] # Stores: ((adj_x, adj_y), required_facing_dir)\n  # Iterate over possible relative positions of an adjacent cell to the workshop\n  for dx, dy in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]: # Check all four direct neighbors\n      adj_x, adj_y = workshop_pos[0] + dx, workshop_pos[1] + dy\n      \n      # Determine the direction the agent needs to face to interact with the workshop\n      # when standing at (adj_x, adj_y).\n      required_facing_dir = None\n      if dx == -1: required_facing_dir = RIGHT # If adj_cell is left of workshop, agent faces right\n      elif dx == 1: required_facing_dir = LEFT # If adj_cell is right of workshop, agent faces left\n      elif dy == -1: required_facing_dir = UP   # If adj_cell is below workshop, agent faces up\n      elif dy == 1: required_facing_dir = DOWN # If adj_cell is above workshop, agent faces down\n      \n      # Check if the adjacent cell is within bounds, is empty, and is not a boundary wall.\n      # `current_state.grid[adj_x, adj_y, :].any()` checks if *any* item is at this location.\n      # If it's 0, the cell is empty.\n      # We also must ensure it's not a boundary, as boundaries are considered \"occupied\" by the boundary object.\n      is_in_bounds = (0 <= adj_x < WIDTH and 0 <= adj_y < HEIGHT)\n      if is_in_bounds:\n          is_empty_of_objects = not current_state.grid[adj_x, adj_y, :].any()\n          is_not_boundary = (current_state.grid[adj_x, adj_y, cookbook.index[\"boundary\"]] == 0)\n      else:\n          is_empty_of_objects = False # Out of bounds is not \"empty\" for pathfinding\n          is_not_boundary = False\n\n      if is_in_bounds and is_empty_of_objects and is_not_boundary:\n          target_adj_cells_info.append(((adj_x, adj_y), required_facing_dir))\n\n  # If no valid adjacent and empty cells are found, cannot reach the workshop.\n  if not target_adj_cells_info:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to an\n  # appropriate crafting spot (adjacent cell with correct orientation).\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here, agent_direction_at_this_position)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [], start_dir)])\n  # The visited set stores: ((position_x, position_y), agent_direction_at_that_pos)\n  # This prevents redundant exploration of the same state (position + direction).\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)} \n\n  path_to_craft_spot = None # This will store (list_of_actions, final_required_direction_at_craft_spot)\n\n  while queue:\n      (x, y), path, agent_dir = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current (position, direction) matches any of our target crafting spots.\n      for (target_x, target_y), required_dir in target_adj_cells_info:\n          if (x, y) == (target_x, target_y) and agent_dir == required_dir:\n              path_to_craft_spot = (path, required_dir)\n              break # Found a valid path, exit inner loop\n      if path_to_craft_spot:\n          break # Found a valid path, exit outer BFS loop\n\n      # Explore possible next moves (actions) from the current state.\n      for action, (dx, dy) in move_actions_map.items():\n          next_x, next_y = x + dx, y + dy\n          \n          # Simulate the outcome of taking 'action':\n          # The agent's direction always changes to the 'action' taken, regardless of movement success.\n          sim_next_dir = action \n\n          # Movement is blocked if the target cell is out of bounds or occupied by any object.\n          is_blocked = False\n          if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n              is_blocked = True # Out of bounds\n          elif current_state.grid[next_x, next_y, :].any():\n              # The CraftState.step function states: `if self.grid[n_x, n_y, :].any(): n_x, n_y = x, y`\n              # This means movement is blocked if ANY item is present in the target cell.\n              is_blocked = True\n          \n          # Determine the simulated next position:\n          sim_next_pos = (x, y) # Default: agent stays put if blocked\n          if not is_blocked:\n              sim_next_pos = (next_x, next_y) # Agent successfully moves\n\n          # If this simulated new state (position + direction) hasn't been visited, add it to the queue.\n          if (sim_next_pos, sim_next_dir) not in visited:\n              visited.add((sim_next_pos, sim_next_dir))\n              queue.append((sim_next_pos, path + [action], sim_next_dir))\n\n  # If no path to a valid crafting spot (with correct orientation) was found, return current total_reward.\n  if not path_to_craft_spot:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Extract the sequence of actions to take from the found path.\n  path_actions, _ = path_to_craft_spot\n\n  # 6. Execute the determined movement actions in the environment.\n  for action in path_actions:\n      reward, _, _ = env.step(action)\n      total_reward += reward\n      # The env._current_state is automatically updated by env.step(),\n      # so subsequent steps in this function will operate on the new state.\n\n  # At this point, the agent is at the correct position adjacent to the workshop\n  # and is facing the correct direction, as ensured by the BFS.\n\n  # 7. Execute the USE action to craft the item.\n  reward, _, _ = env.step(USE)\n  total_reward += reward\n\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-23T23:05:37.029508", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  # Constants defined locally for clarity, derived from the Craft environment code base.\n  WIDTH = 12\n  HEIGHT = 12\n\n  DOWN = 0\n  UP = 1\n  LEFT = 2\n  RIGHT = 3\n  USE = 4\n\n  total_reward = 0.0\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # 1. Get the item's index from the cookbook and retrieve its recipe.\n  # The 'item' argument is expected to be a string name (e.g., \"plank\", \"axe\").\n  # The cookbook.index[] converts these names to integer indices.\n  item_idx = cookbook.index.get(item)\n  if item_idx is None:\n      # Item name not recognized in cookbook.\n      return total_reward\n  \n  # If there's no recipe for the requested item, it cannot be crafted.\n  if item_idx not in cookbook.recipes:\n      return total_reward\n\n  recipe = cookbook.recipes[item_idx]\n\n  # 2. Check if the agent possesses all necessary ingredients for the recipe.\n  current_state = env._current_state # Get the current state of the environment\n  ingredients_ok = True\n  for ingredient_idx, count in recipe.items():\n      # Ingredients are identified by integer indices; special keys like \"_at\" or \"_yield\" are strings.\n      if isinstance(ingredient_idx, int):\n          if current_state.inventory[ingredient_idx] < count:\n              ingredients_ok = False\n              break\n  \n  # If ingredients are missing, crafting cannot proceed.\n  if not ingredients_ok:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # 3. Identify the specific workshop required for crafting this item.\n  # Recipes typically have an \"_at\" key specifying the workshop.\n  if \"_at\" not in recipe:\n      # If no workshop is specified in the recipe, this crafting logic does not apply.\n      return total_reward \n\n  workshop_name = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  workshop_idx = cookbook.index.get(workshop_name)\n  if workshop_idx is None:\n      # Workshop name not recognized in cookbook.\n      return total_reward\n\n  # 4. Locate the workshop's position on the grid.\n  workshop_pos = None\n  for x_grid in range(WIDTH):\n      for y_grid in range(HEIGHT):\n          # Check if the workshop item is at this grid position\n          if current_state.grid[x_grid, y_grid, workshop_idx] == 1:\n              workshop_pos = (x_grid, y_grid)\n              break\n      if workshop_pos: # Workshop found, exit outer loop\n          break\n  \n  # If the required workshop is not present in the current grid, crafting is impossible.\n  if not workshop_pos:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # 5. Pathfinding to an empty cell adjacent to the workshop, ensuring the agent faces it correctly.\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Initial direction of the agent\n  \n  # Define possible movement actions and their corresponding (dx, dy) vectors.\n  move_actions_map = {\n      DOWN: (0, -1),\n      UP: (0, 1),\n      LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n  \n  # Mapping from (delta_x_from_agent_to_object, delta_y_from_agent_to_object) to required agent facing direction.\n  # Example: if workshop is to the right of the agent (dx=1, dy=0), agent must face RIGHT.\n  facing_directions_map = {\n      (-1, 0): LEFT,\n      (1, 0): RIGHT,\n      (0, -1): DOWN,\n      (0, 1): UP\n  }\n  \n  # Determine all valid target cells adjacent to the workshop, and the direction\n  # the agent needs to face from each of those cells to interact with the workshop.\n  target_adj_cells_info = [] # Stores: ((adj_x, adj_y), required_facing_dir)\n  \n  # Iterate over relative positions to find direct neighbors of the workshop\n  for dx_rel, dy_rel in [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]:\n      adj_x, adj_y = workshop_pos[0] + dx_rel, workshop_pos[1] + dy_rel\n      \n      # Calculate the vector from the agent's potential position (adj_x, adj_y) to the workshop.\n      # This is (-dx_rel, -dy_rel).\n      required_facing_dir = facing_directions_map.get((-dx_rel, -dy_rel))\n      \n      # Skip if this relative position doesn't correspond to a standard direction (shouldn't happen for direct neighbors).\n      if required_facing_dir is None:\n          continue\n      \n      # Check if the adjacent cell is within bounds and is empty (i.e., no other item is there).\n      is_cell_blocked = False\n      if not (0 <= adj_x < WIDTH and 0 <= adj_y < HEIGHT):\n          is_cell_blocked = True # Out of bounds\n      elif current_state.grid[adj_x, adj_y, :].any():\n          # According to CraftState.step, if any item is present, movement is blocked.\n          is_cell_blocked = True\n          \n      # Explicitly check for boundary to prevent agent trying to target/move into it.\n      boundary_idx = cookbook.index.get(\"boundary\")\n      if boundary_idx is not None and current_state.grid[adj_x, adj_y, boundary_idx] == 1:\n          is_cell_blocked = True\n\n      if not is_cell_blocked:\n          target_adj_cells_info.append(((adj_x, adj_y), required_facing_dir))\n\n  # If no valid adjacent and empty cells are found, cannot reach the workshop.\n  if not target_adj_cells_info:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to an\n  # appropriate crafting spot (adjacent cell with correct orientation).\n  # BFS queue stores tuples: (current_position (x,y), list_of_actions_taken, current_agent_direction)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [], start_dir)])\n  # Visited set stores: ((position_x, position_y), agent_direction_at_that_pos)\n  # This prevents redundant exploration of the same state (position + direction).\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)} \n\n  path_to_craft_spot = None # This will store (list_of_actions, final_required_direction_at_craft_spot)\n\n  while queue:\n      (x, y), path, agent_dir = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current (position, direction) matches any of our target crafting spots.\n      for (target_x, target_y), required_dir in target_adj_cells_info:\n          if (x, y) == (target_x, target_y) and agent_dir == required_dir:\n              path_to_craft_spot = (path, required_dir)\n              break # Found a valid path, exit inner loop\n      if path_to_craft_spot:\n          break # Found a valid path, exit outer BFS loop\n\n      # Explore possible next moves (actions) from the current state.\n      for action, (dx, dy) in move_actions_map.items():\n          # Calculate potential next grid position if move is successful\n          potential_next_x, potential_next_y = x + dx, y + dy\n          \n          # The agent's direction always changes to the 'action' taken, regardless of movement success.\n          sim_next_dir = action \n\n          # Determine the actual next position based on environment rules.\n          # CraftState.step function: if grid[n_x, n_y, :].any(), agent stays at (x, y).\n          actual_next_pos = (x, y) # Default: agent stays put if blocked\n          \n          is_move_blocked_by_obstacle = False\n          if not (0 <= potential_next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= potential_next_y < HEIGHT):\n              is_move_blocked_by_obstacle = True # Out of bounds\n          elif current_state.grid[potential_next_x, potential_next_y, :].any():\n              is_move_blocked_by_obstacle = True # Cell is occupied by something.\n\n          if not is_move_blocked_by_obstacle:\n              actual_next_pos = (potential_next_x, potential_next_y) # Agent successfully moves\n\n          # If this simulated new state (position + direction) hasn't been visited, add it to the queue.\n          if (actual_next_pos, sim_next_dir) not in visited:\n              visited.add((actual_next_pos, sim_next_dir))\n              queue.append((actual_next_pos, path + [action], sim_next_dir))\n\n  # If no path to a valid crafting spot (with correct orientation) was found, return current total_reward.\n  if not path_to_craft_spot:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Extract the sequence of actions to take from the found path.\n  path_actions, _ = path_to_craft_spot\n\n  # 6. Execute the determined movement actions in the environment.\n  # The env.step() method internally updates the environment's state.\n  for action in path_actions:\n      reward, _, _ = env.step(action)\n      total_reward += reward\n\n  # At this point, the agent is at the correct position adjacent to the workshop\n  # and is facing the correct direction, as ensured by the BFS.\n\n  # 7. Execute the USE action to craft the item.\n  # This uses the latest state of the environment, which has been updated by the path_actions.\n  reward, _, _ = env.step(USE)\n  total_reward += reward\n\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
