{"timestamp": "2025-07-24T01:07:45.141855", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  total_reward = 0.0\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  item_idx = cookbook.index[item_name]\n\n  # Helper logic to move to an object on the grid and use it.\n  # This function is designed to:\n  # 1. Locate the target item/workshop on the grid.\n  # 2. Navigate the agent to be adjacent to the target.\n  # 3. Orient the agent to face the target.\n  # 4. Perform the USE action.\n  # It updates the total_reward collected during this process.\n  def _move_to_and_use_inlined(target_idx, current_total_reward):\n      # Find the actual grid coordinates of the target item\n      target_pos_on_grid = None\n      current_grid = env._current_state.grid\n      \n      # WIDTH and HEIGHT are global constants imported by CraftWorld and thus available here\n      for x in range(WIDTH): \n          for y in range(HEIGHT):\n              if current_grid[x, y, target_idx] == 1:\n                  target_pos_on_grid = (x, y)\n                  break\n          if target_pos_on_grid:\n              break\n\n      # If the target item is not found on the grid, we cannot interact with it.\n      # This can happen if an ingredient has already been picked up.\n      # For a workshop, it should always be present in a valid scenario.\n      if target_pos_on_grid is None:\n          return current_total_reward\n\n      # A safety break to prevent infinite loops during navigation.\n      MAX_MOVE_ATTEMPTS = 100 \n      attempts = 0\n\n      while attempts < MAX_MOVE_ATTEMPTS:\n          # Check if the environment's step limit has been reached\n          if env._is_done(): \n              return current_total_reward\n\n          current_agent_x, current_agent_y = env._current_state.pos\n\n          # Calculate relative position of the target to the agent\n          dx = target_pos_on_grid[0] - current_agent_x\n          dy = target_pos_on_grid[1] - current_agent_y\n\n          # Determine the action needed to either move closer or face the target\n          action_to_take = -1 \n          if dx == 1: action_to_take = RIGHT # Target is to the right\n          elif dx == -1: action_to_take = LEFT # Target is to the left\n          elif dy == 1: action_to_take = UP # Target is above (Y increases upwards in game)\n          elif dy == -1: action_to_take = DOWN # Target is below (Y decreases downwards in game)\n          \n          # Check if the agent is already in the correct state to perform a USE action:\n          # 1. It must be adjacent to the target (Manhattan distance of 1).\n          # 2. Its current direction must be facing the target.\n          is_adjacent = (abs(dx) + abs(dy) == 1)\n          facing_correctly = (action_to_take != -1 and env._current_state.dir == action_to_take)\n          \n          if is_adjacent and facing_correctly:\n              # Agent is in the correct position and orientation. Ready to USE.\n              break \n\n          # Take a step towards the target or to orient the agent.\n          # The CraftState.step handles movement: if the target cell is occupied,\n          # the agent stays put but its direction will be set correctly.\n          if action_to_take != -1:\n              reward, _, _ = env.step(action_to_take)\n              current_total_reward += reward\n          else:\n              # This case indicates that the agent might be exactly on the target (not expected for pickable items/workshops)\n              # or stuck in a complex environment where simple greedy pathing isn't enough.\n              # We break to prevent an infinite loop.\n              break \n          \n          attempts += 1 # Increment attempt counter\n              \n      # After the loop, the agent should ideally be adjacent and facing the target.\n      # Now, perform the USE action to interact with the target (pick up item or use workshop).\n      reward, _, _ = env.step(USE)\n      current_total_reward += reward\n      \n      return current_total_reward\n\n  # 1. Gather all primitive ingredients required for crafting the target item.\n  # `primitives_for` returns a dictionary mapping primitive item indices to their required counts.\n  needed_primitives = cookbook.primitives_for(item_idx)\n  \n  # Loop to collect ingredients until all necessary items are in the agent's inventory.\n  # This loop continues as long as progress is being made (at least one item picked up)\n  # or until the environment's step limit is reached.\n  progress_made_in_collection_loop = True\n  while progress_made_in_collection_loop and not env._is_done():\n      progress_made_in_collection_loop = False # Assume no progress at the start of each iteration\n      \n      current_inventory = env._current_state.inventory\n      all_ingredients_collected = True\n      \n      # Iterate through the list of needed ingredients to find what's missing.\n      for ing_idx, needed_count in needed_primitives.items():\n          if current_inventory[ing_idx] < needed_count:\n              all_ingredients_collected = False # Mark that not all ingredients are collected yet\n              \n              # Try to collect this missing ingredient.\n              initial_inv_count = current_inventory[ing_idx]\n              \n              # Use the inlined helper to navigate to and \"use\" the ingredient on the grid.\n              total_reward = _move_to_and_use_inlined(ing_idx, total_reward)\n              \n              # Check if a new instance of the item was successfully picked up.\n              if env._current_state.inventory[ing_idx] > initial_inv_count:\n                  progress_made_in_collection_loop = True # Mark that progress was made in this iteration\n\n              # If the environment's step limit is reached during collection, exit immediately.\n              if env._is_done(): \n                  return total_reward\n              \n              # If we successfully collected an item, break from this inner for-loop\n              # to re-evaluate the inventory and decide which item to collect next.\n              # This ensures we always target the *next* most needed item or another instance.\n              if progress_made_in_collection_loop:\n                  break \n\n      # If all ingredients are now in inventory, exit the main collection loop.\n      if all_ingredients_collected:\n          break \n\n      # If no progress was made in collecting any item during this full iteration,\n      # it means no more necessary items are available or reachable. Stop trying to collect.\n      if not progress_made_in_collection_loop:\n          break\n          \n  # 2. Craft the item at the appropriate workshop.\n  # First, check if the goal item has already been obtained (e.g., picked up directly if it's a primitive,\n  # or accidentally crafted/obtained in a previous step).\n  if env._current_state.inventory[item_idx] > 0:\n      return total_reward # Item is already in inventory.\n\n  # Get the name of the workshop required for this recipe from the cookbook.\n  # The '_at' key stores the string name of the workshop (e.g., \"workshop1\").\n  workshop_name = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  workshop_idx = cookbook.index[workshop_name] # Convert workshop name to its index.\n\n  # Move the agent to the workshop's location and use it to perform the crafting action.\n  total_reward = _move_to_and_use_inlined(workshop_idx, total_reward)\n\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-24T01:12:36.695041", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  total_reward = 0.0\n\n  # Get the ID for the target item\n  target_item_id = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n  \n  # Get the recipe for the target item\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes[target_item_id]\n\n  # 1. Collect all necessary ingredients\n  for ingredient_id_or_str, count in recipe.items():\n    # Only process actual ingredients (integer IDs), not special keys like \"_at\" or \"_yield\"\n    if isinstance(ingredient_id_or_str, int):\n      ingredient_id = ingredient_id_or_str\n      ingredient_name = env.world.cookbook.index.get(ingredient_id)\n      \n      # While we don't have enough of this ingredient in inventory, collect more\n      while env._current_state.inventory[ingredient_id] < count:\n        # COLLECT_FUNC is assumed to be an existing DSL function that handles\n        # moving to and picking up the specified kind of item.\n        # It should return the reward collected during its operation.\n        r, _, _ = COLLECT_FUNC(env, ingredient_name)\n        total_reward += r\n\n  # 2. Move to the correct workshop and perform the craft\n  workshop_name = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  workshop_id = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n  \n  # Find the workshop's position on the grid\n  workshop_pos = None\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  width, height, _ = grid.shape\n  for x in range(width):\n      for y in range(height):\n          if grid[x, y, workshop_id] == 1:\n              workshop_pos = (x, y)\n              break\n      if workshop_pos:\n          break\n\n  if workshop_pos is None:\n      # This case indicates the workshop is not present in the environment.\n      # For well-formed scenarios, this should not happen if the item is craftable.\n      # Return current total_reward (likely 0 or from ingredient collection).\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Keep moving until the agent is adjacent to the workshop\n  while not env._current_state.next_to(workshop_id):\n    current_x, current_y = env._current_state.pos\n    wx, wy = workshop_pos\n    \n    # Determine the direction to move: prioritize movement along the axis\n    # with the larger distance to the workshop. This is a simple greedy strategy.\n    if abs(wx - current_x) > abs(wy - current_y):\n      if wx > current_x:\n        # Move RIGHT towards the workshop\n        r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, env_factory.RIGHT)\n      else:\n        # Move LEFT towards the workshop\n        r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, env_factory.LEFT)\n    else: # abs(wx - current_x) <= abs(wy - current_y)\n      if wy > current_y:\n        # Move UP towards the workshop\n        r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, env_factory.UP)\n      else:\n        # Move DOWN towards the workshop\n        r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, env_factory.DOWN)\n    total_reward += r # Add reward from movement\n\n  # At this point, the agent is adjacent to the workshop.\n  # Due to how `CraftState.step` handles collision and updates direction,\n  # the agent should be facing the workshop after the last movement that brought it adjacent.\n  \n  # Perform the USE action to craft the item\n  # env_factory.USE corresponds to the integer action for 'USE'\n  reward_use, _, _ = env.step(env_factory.USE)\n  total_reward += reward_use\n\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-24T01:12:37.756964", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-24T01:26:50.295873", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "    total_reward = 0.0\n    cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n    item_index = cookbook.index[item_name]\n    recipe = cookbook.recipes.get(item_index)\n\n    if not recipe:\n        # If the item is not found in recipes, it cannot be crafted.\n        # This handles cases where item_name might be a primitive or an invalid item.\n        return total_reward\n\n    # 1. Gather ingredients required for the recipe\n    for ingredient_idx, count_needed in recipe.items():\n        if isinstance(ingredient_idx, int):  # It's an ingredient (represented by its index)\n            current_has = env._current_state.inventory[ingredient_idx]\n            to_get = count_needed - current_has\n\n            if to_get > 0:\n                ingredient_name = cookbook.index.get(ingredient_idx)\n                # Determine if the ingredient is a primitive or another craftable item\n                if ingredient_idx in cookbook.primitives:\n                    # If it's a primitive, use COLLECT_FUNC to obtain it\n                    for _ in range(to_get):\n                        # Assuming COLLECT_FUNC(env, kind_name) is globally available\n                        # and handles navigation and item pickup.\n                        r, _, _ = COLLECT_FUNC(env, ingredient_name)\n                        total_reward += r\n                        # Break if the item is collected (or if COLLECT_FUNC cannot get it)\n                        if env._current_state.inventory[ingredient_idx] >= count_needed:\n                            break\n                else:\n                    # If it's another craftable item, recursively call CRAFT_FUNC\n                    for _ in range(to_get):\n                        # CRAFT_FUNC(env, item_name) is the function being implemented itself.\n                        r, _, _ = CRAFT_FUNC(env, ingredient_name)\n                        total_reward += r\n                        # Break if the item is crafted\n                        if env._current_state.inventory[ingredient_idx] >= count_needed:\n                            break\n    \n    # After attempting to gather all ingredients, check if we have them.\n    # If not, we might not be able to proceed with crafting.\n    for ingredient_idx, count_needed in recipe.items():\n        if isinstance(ingredient_idx, int):\n            if env._current_state.inventory[ingredient_idx] < count_needed:\n                # Could not gather all ingredients, so cannot craft.\n                return total_reward\n\n    # 2. Move to the specific workshop required for crafting (if any)\n    workshop_name = recipe.get('_at')\n    if workshop_name:\n        workshop_index = cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n        \n        # Find the exact coordinates of the workshop on the grid\n        workshop_loc = None\n        grid = env._current_state.grid\n        for x_grid in range(WIDTH): # WIDTH and HEIGHT are assumed global constants from Craft environment\n            for y_grid in range(HEIGHT):\n                if grid[x_grid, y_grid, workshop_index] == 1:\n                    workshop_loc = (x_grid, y_grid)\n                    break\n            if workshop_loc:\n                break\n        \n        if not workshop_loc:\n            # Workshop not found on the map, cannot craft.\n            return total_reward\n\n        # Navigate agent to a position immediately adjacent to the workshop\n        target_x, target_y = workshop_loc\n        current_agent_x, current_agent_y = env._current_state.pos\n\n        # Maximum steps for navigation to prevent infinite loops.\n        # A heuristic based on grid size.\n        max_nav_steps = WIDTH * HEIGHT * 2 \n        steps_taken = 0\n        \n        # Loop until the agent is adjacent to the workshop or max steps exceeded\n        # A position (ax,ay) is adjacent to (tx,ty) if abs(ax-tx) + abs(ay-ty) == 1\n        while (abs(current_agent_x - target_x) + abs(current_agent_y - target_y) != 1) and steps_taken < max_nav_steps:\n            moved_in_step = False\n            # Prioritize horizontal movement, then vertical to reduce zigzagging\n            if current_agent_x < target_x:\n                r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, \"RIGHT\") # Assuming MOVE_FUNC(env, dir_str) is globally available\n                total_reward += r\n                moved_in_step = True\n            elif current_agent_x > target_x:\n                r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, \"LEFT\")\n                total_reward += r\n                moved_in_step = True\n            elif current_agent_y < target_y:\n                r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, \"UP\")\n                total_reward += r\n                moved_in_step = True\n            elif current_agent_y > target_y:\n                r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, \"DOWN\")\n                total_reward += r\n                moved_in_step = True\n            \n            new_agent_x, new_agent_y = env._current_state.pos\n            if new_agent_x == current_agent_x and new_agent_y == current_agent_y and moved_in_step:\n                # Agent tried to move but was blocked (e.g., by boundary or another object).\n                # Cannot reach workshop, so stop trying.\n                break \n            \n            current_agent_x, current_agent_y = new_agent_x, new_agent_y\n            steps_taken += 1\n        \n        # After navigation, verify adjacency. If not adjacent, something went wrong (e.g., blocked path).\n        if (abs(current_agent_x - target_x) + abs(current_agent_y - target_y) != 1):\n            return total_reward\n\n        # Once adjacent to the workshop, ensure the agent is facing it.\n        # The `USE` action in CraftState.step checks `neighbors(self.pos, self.dir)`.\n        agent_x, agent_y = env._current_state.pos\n        current_dir = env._current_state.dir\n\n        # Adjust direction to face the workshop's location.\n        # These actions also contribute to total_reward and may cause minor movement if path is clear.\n        if target_x == agent_x + 1 and current_dir != RIGHT:\n            r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, \"RIGHT\") \n            total_reward += r\n        elif target_x == agent_x - 1 and current_dir != LEFT:\n            r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, \"LEFT\")\n            total_reward += r\n        elif target_y == agent_y + 1 and current_dir != UP:\n            r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, \"UP\")\n            total_reward += r\n        elif target_y == agent_y - 1 and current_dir != DOWN:\n            r, _, _ = MOVE_FUNC(env, \"DOWN\")\n            total_reward += r\n        # If agent is already facing the correct direction, no action is needed to change direction.\n\n    # 3. Perform the USE action to attempt crafting\n    # This action consumes ingredients and produces the item if conditions are met\n    # (i.e., ingredients in inventory, agent at correct location and facing correctly).\n    r, done, observations = env.step(env.action_specs()[\"USE\"])\n    total_reward += r\n    \n    # The accumulated `total_reward` reflects all sub-actions\n    # (collecting ingredients, moving, and the final USE action).\n    # The CraftLab._get_reward method (part of the environment) determines\n    # the specific reward for obtaining the goal item or intermediate items.\n    return total_reward", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
