{"timestamp": "2025-07-24T01:35:08.834142", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  total_reward = 0.0\n\n  # 1. Get the target item's index.\n  # Item is typically a string, e.g., \"plank\"\n  item_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n\n  # 2. Get the recipe for the item to find the required workshop.\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(item_idx)\n  if recipe is None:\n    # Item cannot be crafted or doesn't exist as a recipe output\n    return total_reward\n\n  workshop_name = recipe.get('_at')\n  if workshop_name is None:\n    # Item might be a primitive, not craftable at a specific workshop,\n    # or the recipe does not specify a workshop.\n    # For the 'craft' function, we assume a workshop is involved.\n    return total_reward\n\n  # 3. Find the coordinates of the required workshop in the current grid.\n  workshop_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n  \n  # Find all instances of the workshop in the current grid\n  workshop_coords = np.argwhere(env._current_state.grid[:, :, workshop_idx] == 1)\n\n  if len(workshop_coords) == 0:\n    # Workshop not found in the current grid\n    return total_reward\n  \n  # For simplicity, target the first found workshop\n  workshop_x, workshop_y = workshop_coords[0]\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  ACTIONS = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = ACTIONS['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = ACTIONS['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = ACTIONS['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = ACTIONS['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = ACTIONS['USE']\n\n  # Phase 1: Move adjacent to the workshop.\n  # This loop will continue until the agent is adjacent to the workshop\n  # or the environment signals done (e.g., max_steps is reached).\n  # We use a safety break to prevent infinite loops in complex scenarios.\n  max_loop_steps = env.max_steps \n  steps_taken = 0\n  \n  while not env._current_state.next_to(workshop_idx) and steps_taken < max_loop_steps:\n    curr_x, curr_y = env._current_state.pos\n    action_to_take = -1 # Initialize with an invalid action\n\n    # Determine movement action towards the workshop.\n    # Prioritize moving in X direction first, then Y, to provide a consistent path.\n    if curr_x < workshop_x:\n      action_to_take = ACTION_RIGHT\n    elif curr_x > workshop_x:\n      action_to_take = ACTION_LEFT\n    elif curr_y < workshop_y:\n      action_to_take = ACTION_UP\n    elif curr_y > workshop_y:\n      action_to_take = ACTION_DOWN\n    else:\n        # Agent is at the same (x,y) as the workshop. This should not happen\n        # if workshops are impassable, but implies being \"on\" the workshop.\n        # If it happens, we assume it's already in a position to use.\n        # This break ensures we don't get stuck if no valid movement is found\n        # to become adjacent.\n        break \n\n    reward, done, _ = env.step(action_to_take)\n    total_reward += reward\n    steps_taken += 1\n    \n    if done:\n      # If the task is completed or failed (e.g., ran out of steps) during movement\n      return total_reward \n\n  # Check if agent successfully moved adjacent to the workshop\n  if not env._current_state.next_to(workshop_idx):\n      # Could not get adjacent to the workshop after trying.\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Phase 2: Face the workshop.\n  # The agent is now adjacent to the workshop. We need to turn to face it.\n  curr_x, curr_y = env._current_state.pos\n  \n  dx = workshop_x - curr_x\n  dy = workshop_y - curr_y\n\n  target_dir_action = -1\n  if dx == 1: # Workshop is to the right of the agent\n    target_dir_action = ACTION_RIGHT\n  elif dx == -1: # Workshop is to the left of the agent\n    target_dir_action = ACTION_LEFT\n  elif dy == 1: # Workshop is above the agent (in y-coord sense)\n    target_dir_action = ACTION_UP\n  elif dy == -1: # Workshop is below the agent\n    target_dir_action = ACTION_DOWN\n  \n  # If the agent is not already facing the target direction, perform a step\n  # in that direction. The agent's position will not change if blocked,\n  # but its direction will update.\n  if env._current_state.dir != target_dir_action and target_dir_action != -1:\n    reward, done, _ = env.step(target_dir_action)\n    total_reward += reward\n    if done:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Phase 3: Use the workshop.\n  # Agent is adjacent to the workshop and facing it. Perform the USE action.\n  reward, done, _ = env.step(ACTION_USE)\n  total_reward += reward\n  \n  if done:\n    return total_reward\n\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
