{"timestamp": "2025-07-24T05:15:05.915187", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Helper function to move to a target kind (object/station on grid) and then attempt to use it.\n  # This function encapsulates the navigation and interaction logic, updating the environment state\n  # and accumulating reward in the outer scope's `total_reward`.\n  def _move_to_and_use(target_kind_idx):\n      nonlocal total_reward # Allows modification of total_reward from the outer `craft_v1` scope\n      \n      current_state = env._current_state\n\n      # Find the target on the grid. `np.where` returns a tuple of arrays (x_coords, y_coords).\n      target_locs = np.where(current_state.grid[:, :, target_kind_idx] == 1)\n      \n      # If no instances of the target kind are found on the grid, it means it's\n      # either already collected, not present, or unreachable. In such cases,\n      # no action can be taken towards it, so the function simply returns.\n      if len(target_locs[0]) == 0:\n          return\n\n      # Use the first found instance of the target as the destination.\n      target_x, target_y = target_locs[0][0], target_locs[1][0]\n\n      # Phase 1: Move towards the target position\n      # Loop continues until the agent's current position matches the target's coordinates.\n      while env._current_state.pos != (target_x, target_y):\n          cx, cy = env._current_state.pos\n          action = -1 # Initialize action to an invalid value\n\n          # Determine the appropriate movement action (UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT)\n          # based on the current position relative to the target.\n          # Note on Y-axis: In CraftWorld, increasing Y means moving \"up\" on the map.\n          if cx < target_x:\n              action = RIGHT # Move right to increase X\n          elif cx > target_x:\n              action = LEFT  # Move left to decrease X\n          elif cy < target_y: # If target Y is greater, move UP\n              action = UP\n          elif cy > target_y: # If target Y is smaller, move DOWN\n              action = DOWN\n          \n          # If a valid movement action was determined, execute it in the environment.\n          if action != -1:\n              # `env.step` returns (reward, done, observations).\n              # `reward` here is the immediate step reward as determined by CraftLab's `_get_reward`.\n              reward, done, _ = env.step(action)\n              total_reward += reward # Accumulate the reward\n              \n              # If the environment signals `done` (e.g., max_steps reached or goal achieved),\n              # no further actions are needed for this task, so return immediately.\n              if done: \n                  return \n          else:\n              # This condition should ideally only be met if the agent is already at the target.\n              # If not, it implies the agent is stuck or unable to move, so break the loop to prevent infinite loop.\n              break \n\n      # Phase 2: Once the agent is at the target's coordinates, attempt to USE it.\n      # This action can pick up items, activate workshops for crafting, or interact with environmental features.\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(USE)\n      total_reward += reward # Accumulate reward from the USE action\n      \n      # Check again if the task is done after the USE action.\n      if done:\n          return\n\n  # --- Main logic for the `craft_v1` function starts here ---\n  \n  # Retrieve the integer index corresponding to the `item` string (e.g., \"plank\", \"axe\").\n  goal_item_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n\n  # Before attempting to craft, check if the item is indeed craftable according to the cookbook.\n  # The `craft` function in the DSL implies that the item should have a defined recipe.\n  if goal_item_idx not in env.world.cookbook.recipes:\n      # If the item has no recipe, it cannot be crafted using this method.\n      # Return the accumulated reward (which will be 0 in this case, as no steps were taken for crafting).\n      return total_reward\n\n  # Get the recipe details for the item to be crafted.\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes[goal_item_idx]\n\n  # Identify all ultimate primitive ingredients required to craft the final item.\n  # The `cookbook.primitives_for` method recursively resolves all sub-recipes to\n  # provide a list of base (primitive) materials and their total required counts.\n  ultimate_primitives = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(goal_item_idx)\n\n  # Phase 1: Collect all necessary primitive ingredients.\n  # Iterate through each required primitive item and its total count.\n  for p_idx, p_count in list(ultimate_primitives.items()): # `list()` creates a copy for safe iteration\n      # Before attempting to collect, check if the overall task is already done.\n      # This can happen if `max_steps` is reached during previous actions or if goal was met unexpectedly.\n      if env._is_done():\n          break # Exit the loop if the task is already completed.\n      \n      # Continuously try to collect this primitive until the required count is met in the agent's inventory.\n      while env._current_state.inventory[p_idx] < p_count:\n          # Use the helper function to navigate to and interact with the primitive.\n          _move_to_and_use(p_idx)\n          \n          # After each attempt to collect, re-check the `done` status.\n          # This is crucial for stopping early if `max_steps` is hit or the goal is satisfied.\n          if env._is_done():\n              break # Exit if the task is done\n\n  # Phase 2: Move to the designated crafting station and perform the crafting action.\n  crafting_station_idx = None\n  \n  # Craftable item recipes typically specify the workshop required via the \"_at\" key.\n  if \"_at\" in recipe:\n      station_name = recipe[\"_at\"]\n      crafting_station_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[station_name]\n  \n  # If a specific crafting station is identified, navigate to it and use it.\n  if crafting_station_idx is not None:\n      # Only proceed with the final crafting step if the task is not already done.\n      if not env._is_done():\n          _move_to_and_use(crafting_station_idx)\n          \n  # Return the total accumulated reward from all steps taken throughout the crafting process.\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
