{"timestamp": "2025-07-24T07:04:54.706072", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  total_reward = 0.0\n\n  # Define constants from the environment logic locally for self-containment\n  WIDTH = 12\n  HEIGHT = 12\n  DOWN = 0\n  UP = 1\n  LEFT = 2\n  RIGHT = 3\n  USE = 4\n\n  # 1. Get the integer index for the target item\n  target_item_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n\n  # 2. Retrieve the recipe for the target item from the cookbook\n  # If the item is not found in recipes, it's not craftable through this mechanism.\n  if target_item_idx not in env.world.cookbook.recipes:\n    return total_reward\n\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes[target_item_idx]\n\n  # 3. Identify the required crafting station (workshop) from the recipe\n  # Craftable items typically specify which workshop they are crafted \"_at\".\n  if \"_at\" not in recipe:\n    return total_reward # Cannot craft without a specified workshop\n\n  workshop_name = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  workshop_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n\n  # 4. Find the exact coordinates of the workshop on the grid\n  workshop_pos = None\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  for x_grid in range(WIDTH):\n    for y_grid in range(HEIGHT):\n      if grid[x_grid, y_grid, workshop_idx] == 1:\n        workshop_pos = (x_grid, y_grid)\n        break\n    if workshop_pos: # Found the workshop\n      break\n\n  if not workshop_pos:\n    return total_reward # Workshop not found in the current grid\n\n  # 5. Determine a suitable adjacent position for the agent to stand for crafting\n  target_agent_pos = None\n  wx, wy = workshop_pos\n  # Define possible relative positions (neighbors) around the workshop\n  possible_relative_agent_positions = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)] \n  \n  for dx, dy in possible_relative_agent_positions:\n    nx, ny = wx + dx, wy + dy\n    # Check if the potential position is within grid boundaries\n    if 0 <= nx < WIDTH and 0 <= ny < HEIGHT:\n      # Check if the spot is empty (no other object, including boundary, is there)\n      if not grid[nx, ny, :].any():\n        target_agent_pos = (nx, ny)\n        break\n\n  if not target_agent_pos:\n    return total_reward # No empty spot found next to the workshop\n\n  # 6. Move the agent to the `target_agent_pos`\n  current_agent_pos = env._current_state.pos\n  max_move_attempts = WIDTH * HEIGHT * 2 # Safety break to prevent infinite loops\n\n  attempts = 0\n  while current_agent_pos != target_agent_pos and attempts < max_move_attempts:\n    ax, ay = current_agent_pos\n    tx, ty = target_agent_pos\n\n    action_to_take = -1 # Initialize with an invalid action\n    \n    # Prioritize moving horizontally, then vertically (simple pathfinding)\n    if tx > ax: # Need to move right\n      action_to_take = RIGHT\n    elif tx < ax: # Need to move left\n      action_to_take = LEFT\n    elif ty > ay: # Need to move up (Y increases upwards in CraftWorld)\n      action_to_take = UP\n    elif ty < ay: # Need to move down (Y decreases downwards in CraftWorld)\n      action_to_take = DOWN\n    else:\n      # Agent is already at the target_agent_pos, break\n      break \n\n    # If a valid action was determined, execute it\n    if action_to_take != -1:\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(action_to_take)\n      total_reward += reward\n      if done: \n        # Environment reset or max steps reached, return accumulated reward\n        return total_reward\n      \n      current_agent_pos = env._current_state.pos # Update agent's actual position\n    else:\n      # No valid action could move the agent closer, likely stuck\n      break\n    \n    attempts += 1 # Increment attempts counter\n\n  # If agent failed to reach the target position after maximum attempts\n  if current_agent_pos != target_agent_pos:\n      return total_reward\n\n  # 7. Orient the agent to face the workshop\n  # Agent is now at target_agent_pos.\n  ax, ay = current_agent_pos\n  wx, wy = workshop_pos\n\n  direction_to_face = -1\n  if wx == ax - 1 and wy == ay: # Workshop is to the left of the agent\n    direction_to_face = LEFT\n  elif wx == ax + 1 and wy == ay: # Workshop is to the right of the agent\n    direction_to_face = RIGHT\n  elif wy == ay - 1 and wx == ax: # Workshop is below the agent (smaller Y coordinate)\n    direction_to_face = DOWN\n  elif wy == ay + 1 and wx == ax: # Workshop is above the agent (larger Y coordinate)\n    direction_to_face = UP\n\n  # Only change direction if the agent isn't already facing the correct way and a valid direction was found\n  if direction_to_face != -1 and env._current_state.dir != direction_to_face:\n    # Taking a directional step action will update the agent's direction\n    # even if its position doesn't change (e.g., due to being blocked).\n    reward, done, obs = env.step(direction_to_face)\n    total_reward += reward\n    if done: \n      return total_reward\n\n  # 8. Perform the USE action to craft the item\n  reward, done, obs = env.step(USE)\n  total_reward += reward\n  if done: \n    return total_reward\n\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
