{"timestamp": "2025-07-24T09:41:57.190950", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  total_reward = 0.0\n\n  # Constants for actions\n  DOWN = 0\n  UP = 1\n  LEFT = 2\n  RIGHT = 3\n  USE = 4\n\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  item_id = cookbook.index[item]\n\n  # 1. Check if the item is craftable and has a workshop recipe\n  if item_id not in cookbook.recipes:\n    return 0.0\n\n  recipe = cookbook.recipes[item_id]\n  workshop_name = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n\n  if not workshop_name:\n    # If '_at' key is missing, it's not a workshop-based crafting recipe\n    return 0.0\n\n  workshop_id = cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n\n  # 2. Find the workshop's location (x,y) on the grid\n  workshop_pos = None\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      if grid[x, y, workshop_id] == 1:\n        workshop_pos = (x, y)\n        break\n    if workshop_pos:\n      break\n\n  if not workshop_pos:\n    # Workshop not found on the current grid\n    return 0.0\n\n  # 3. Move to the workshop until adjacent and then attempt to craft\n  # Use max_steps from the environment as a safeguard to prevent infinite loops\n  # Add 1 for the potential final USE action\n  max_operation_steps = env.max_steps\n\n  for _ in range(max_operation_steps + 1):\n    # Check if the environment indicates the episode is done (e.g., goal achieved or max steps reached)\n    if env._is_done():\n      break\n\n    current_state = env._current_state\n\n    # Check if the agent is currently adjacent to the workshop\n    if current_state.next_to(workshop_id):\n      # If adjacent, attempt to craft by performing the 'USE' action\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(USE)\n      total_reward += reward\n      # If the 'USE' action results in the episode being done, break the loop\n      if done:\n        break\n      # Assuming one attempt to USE after reaching the workshop is sufficient for v1.\n      break\n    \n    # If not adjacent, determine the next movement action to get closer to the workshop\n    cx, cy = current_state.pos\n    tx, ty = workshop_pos\n\n    action_to_take = -1\n\n    # Simple greedy movement: prioritize horizontal movement, then vertical\n    # The step function handles staying in place if the move is into an occupied cell.\n    if cx < tx:\n      action_to_take = RIGHT\n    elif cx > tx:\n      action_to_take = LEFT\n    elif cy < ty:\n      action_to_take = UP\n    elif cy > ty:\n      action_to_take = DOWN\n    # If cx == tx and cy == ty, this case implies the agent is at the workshop's position,\n    # which is generally not allowed by the game's movement rules (workshops are obstacles).\n    # If it somehow gets there, it should stop moving and rely on `next_to` or max_steps.\n    # We implicitly assume it will be adjacent.\n\n    if action_to_take != -1:\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(action_to_take)\n      total_reward += reward\n      if done:\n        break\n    # If no action was taken (action_to_take remains -1), it means the agent is\n    # either on the workshop (shouldn't happen with proper env setup) or\n    # cannot move closer with simple greedy moves (e.g., blocked).\n    # The loop will eventually terminate by max_operation_steps.\n\n  return total_reward", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
